     "content": "### The Short Answer\n\n**Yes, you should strongly lean toward taking it.** \n\nA **$200,000 sign-on bonus** completely changes the math. Google effectively gave you a 1:1 cash replacement for your unvested Meta cliff on top of an already solid grant. This shifts the offer from a lateral move into a **top-of-market package** for an L6 PM.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Financial Breakdown (4-Year Picture)\n\nHere is what your actual compensation trajectory looks like compared to staying at Meta:\n\n| Year | Meta (Estimated) | Google Revised Offer | Difference |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | ~$526,000 | **~$758,000** *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Equity $270k + Sign-on $200k)* | **+$232,000 (+44%)** |\n| **Year 2** | ~$530,000 | **~$620,000** *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Init. Equity $270k + Refresh $62.5k)* | **+$90,000** |\n| **Year 3** | ~$535,000 | **~$683,000** *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Init. Equity $270k + Refresh $125k)* | **+$148,000** |\n| **Year 4** | ~$540,000 | **~$745,000** *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Init. Equity $270k + Refresh $187.5k)* | **+$205,000** |\n| **4-Year Total** | **~$2.13M** | **~$2.80M** | **+$670,000+ (~$168k/yr avg surplus)** |\n\n*(Note: Assumes Google standard refresh stacking illustration of ~$250k/4yr per cycle and stable stock prices. Even with zero refreshes, Year 1 alone gives you an extra $232,000 in liquid compensation).*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is a Compelling Offer\n\n1. **Guaranteed Cash Upside:** The $200,000 sign-on bonus is liquid cash that does not depend on performance ratings or stock volatility in Year 1.\n2. **De-risked Transition:** The biggest risk of leaving a company where you are well-regarded is walking away from vested momentum. The sign-on bonus fully insulates you against that risk.\n3. **Band Position:** At ~$758k Year 1 TC, you are at the upper percentile of Google L6 PM compensation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\nBefore you verbally accept, ask the recruiter to clarify three specific items:\n\n1. **Sign-on Bonus Payout & Clawback:**\n   * Is the $200,000 paid as a lump sum in your first paycheck, or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k/$100k)? *(Lump sum in Year 1 is standard, but verify).*\n   * What is the clawback policy? *(Usually pro-rated if you leave before 12 months).*\n2. **Equity Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm if the $1.08M grant vests evenly (25% per year) or on Google's front-loaded schedule (e.g., 33% / 33% / 22% / 12% or 38% / 32% / 20% / 10%). If it is front-loaded, your Year 1 and Year 2 compensation will be **even higher** than the numbers above.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Final Decision Matrix\n\n* **Take the offer if:** You want to add Google L6 to your resume, secure an extra ~$670k+ over 4 years, and are comfortable with the usual PM culture shift (Meta tends to be top-down and execution/velocity-heavy; Google tends to be consensus-driven and engineering-heavy).\n* **Stay at Meta only if:** You are on an immediate fast-track to Director/IC7 (where L7 comp exceeds $800k\u2013$1M+), or you genuinely dislike the product area/team you would be joining at Google.",
